      "side": 1,
      "message": "Greg is right. These features need to be submitted upstream. This patch should be refactored to avoid special code for a particular device but add support for the overcurrent and special port behavior. Presumably there is some quirk mechanisms that can be used. There should be separate patches for the overcurrent change and port behavior change.\n\nThis will take some time, so in the meantime, this patch can be refactored to use vendor hooks instead of changing the behavior. I\u0027ve added comments to suggest how to do this... but please pursue the upstream changes so that next year it is done properly.\n\nDocumentation on vendor hooks and ANDROID_OEM_DATA(): https://preview.source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/kernel/kernel-code#vendor-hooks",
